# The licensed and proprietary corpus and everything derived from it must never
# be uploaded to a public deployment. The public tier runs without a knowledge
# base by design; these entries make that structural rather than a matter of care.
knowledge-source/
# Anchored to the repository root: an unanchored "data/" also matched
# knowledge/medications/data (the medication identity index, which must ship).
/data/
# authored/ holds the project author's OWN material (the quality & defect
# corpus from his manual). It is not licensed third-party content and it SHIPS.
# Keeping it outside data/ means the deny rule above stays absolute — no
# negation to get wrong, no way to leak the licensed corpus by reordering.
# authored/gmai_clinical_v2 and public/clinical-v2 (emergency / ICU clinical
# knowledge, package GMAI-CLINICAL-KNOWLEDGE-L5-v2) were provided by the owner
# for this app and ship too. The package's train/validation files are never
# imported (scripts/import-clinical-v2.mjs).
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
/mnt
*.zip
GAUSHVI.bat
screenshots/
